WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:06.640
Let's start to formalize the problem of learning a good word embedding.
When you implement an algorithm to

2
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.230
learn a word embedding, what you end up learning is an

3
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.698
embedding matrix. Let's take a look at what that means.

4
00:00:12.698 --> 00:00:14.285
Let's say, as usual we're using

5
00:00:14.285 --> 00:00:19.005
our 10,000-word vocabulary. So, the vocabulary has A,

6
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:21.412
Aaron, Orange, Zulu, maybe also unknown word as a token.

7
00:00:21.412 --> 00:00:29.750
What we're going to do is

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.475
learn embedding matrix E, which is going

9
00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:43.900
to be a 300 dimensional by 10,000 dimensional matrix, if you have 10,000 words vocabulary

10
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.933
or maybe 10,001 is unknown word token,there's one extra token.

11
00:00:48.933 --> 00:00:51.105
And the columns of this matrix would be the

12
00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:54.675
different embeddings for the

13
00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:58.245
10,000 different words you have in your vocabulary. So, Orange was word number

14
00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:05.475
6257 in our vocabulary of 10,000 words. So, one piece of notation

15
00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:12.300
we'll use is that 06257 was the one-hot vector with

16
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:18.995
zeros everywhere and a one in position 6257. And so, this will be a

17
00:01:20.995 --> 00:01:25.690
10,000-dimensional vector with a one in just one position.

18
00:01:25.690 --> 00:01:29.430
So, this isn't quite a drawn scale. Yes, this should be as tall

19
00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.220
as the embedding matrix on the left is wide.

20
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:39.930
And if the embedding matrix is called capital E then notice that if you take E

21
00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:46.140
and multiply it by just one-hot vector by 0 of 6257,

22
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:52.045
then this will be a 300-dimensional vector.

23
00:01:52.045 --> 00:02:00.170
So, E is 300 by 10,000 and 0 is 10,000 by 1.

24
00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:05.700
So, the product will be 300 by 1,

25
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.060
so with 300-dimensional vector and notice that

26
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.840
to compute the first element of this vector,

27
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.385
of this 300-dimensional vector,

28
00:02:14.385 --> 00:02:19.565
what you do is you will multiply the first row of the matrix E with this.

29
00:02:19.565 --> 00:02:22.535
But all of these elements are zero except for

30
00:02:22.535 --> 00:02:26.970
element 6257 and so you end up with zero times this,

31
00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:29.490
zero times this, zero times this, and so on.

32
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.270
And then, 1 times whatever this is,

33
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:35.060
and zero times this, zero times this, zero times and so on.

34
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:42.350
And so, you end up with the first element as whatever is that elements up there,

35
00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.235
under the Orange column.

36
00:02:44.235 --> 00:02:48.169
And then, for the second element of this 300-dimensional vector we're computing,

37
00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:50.210
you would take the vector

38
00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:57.055
0657 and multiply it by the second row with the matrix E. So again,

39
00:02:57.055 --> 00:02:58.010
you have zero times this,

40
00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.835
plus zero times this,

41
00:03:00.835 --> 00:03:05.855
plus zero times all of these are the elements and then one times this,

42
00:03:05.855 --> 00:03:09.330
and then zero times everything else and add that together.

43
00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:17.795
So you end up with this and so on as you go down the rest of this column.

44
00:03:17.795 --> 00:03:23.485
So, that's why the embedding matrix E times this one-hot vector here winds up

45
00:03:23.485 --> 00:03:30.430
selecting out this 300-dimensional column corresponding to the word Orange.

46
00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:36.870
So, this is going to be equal to E 6257 which

47
00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.245
is the notation we're going to use to represent

48
00:03:39.245 --> 00:03:43.345
the embedding vector that 300 by one dimensional vector for the word Orange.